{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:0.2", "PA_ja_104:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Parosatavagga (The Chapter on One Hundred and Fifty)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:0.4"], "en": "4. The Mittavindakajātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:1.1", "PA_ja_104:1.2"], "en": "“From four he attained eight, and from eight, sixteen.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:1.3"], "en": "And sixteen and thirty-two—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:1.4"], "en": "excessive desire brings the wheel of suffering upon one;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:1.5"], "en": "for a person overcome by craving, [the cycle turns].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:1.6"], "en": "“A wheel turns upon my head.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_104:2.1"], "en": "The fourth Jātaka, the Mittavindaka Jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
